@@ -7,6 +7,12 @@ Required properties:
 The clock consumer should specify the desired clock by having the clock
 ID in its "clocks" phandle cell (see include/.../pxa-clock.h).
 
+The PXA25x and PXA27x providers expose CLK_CORE for the CPU core and
+CLK_MEMORY for the existing memory-timing reference used by cpufreq. The
+latter keeps its legacy global name ("system_bus" on PXA25x, "memory" on
+PXA27x). It is distinct from the PXA25x internal PXbus affected by fast_bus.
+Clock IDs 0 through 61 retain their original values; CLK_MEMORY is 62.
+
 Examples:
 
 pxa2xx_clks: pxa2xx_clks@41300004 {
